>>__ load "blastLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="words"};
## `BBLAST_TAC`

``` hol4
blastLib.BBLAST_TAC : tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Attempts finite-word goals by Boolean bit-blasting.

`BBLAST_TAC` is `Tactic.CONV_TAC blastLib.BBLAST_CONV`. It applies the
conversion to the goal conclusion, expanding supported word operations
into Boolean formulas. It can close a converted proposition or leave a
residual Boolean goal. If the conversion reports no change, the tactic
succeeds without changing the goal. This brute-force approach is most
useful for small concrete word sizes. Its supported operations and
limitations are those of `BBLAST_CONV`.

Despite the similar name, this tactic is unrelated to
`tableauLib.BLAST_TAC`. `BBLAST_TAC` specializes in finite-word
bit-blasting, whereas `tableauLib.BLAST_TAC` performs general classical
tableau search using a classical rule set.

### Failure

Fails if `BBLAST_CONV` raises an exception. Unsupported operations may
instead remain in an unchanged or residual goal, so success does not by
itself mean that the goal was solved.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem bblast_tac_example:
  !a : word8. a && 0w = 0w
Proof
  blastLib.BBLAST_TAC
QED
```

